  "notes": "The guitar loop is the song. A 4-bar fingerpicked or arpeggiated cell carries the whole harmony, and the two core cycles — i–VI–III–VII and i–VI–VII–V — do most of the work. Toplines are rap-sung: pentatonic skeletons, 2-bar call answered by 2-bar response, and descending 'sighing' contours. The 808 shadows the guitar roots 1:1 and glides for emotion rather than for menace.",

